[I] Backwards compatible callback APIs

[T] backcall is a small Python library for specifying the signature of
[T] callback functions passed in to an API using a prototype function. It
[T] checks supplied callbacks and adapts them, so that new parameters can be
[T] added later without breaking existing callbacks; it is used by IPython.

[U] https://github.com/takluyver/backcall

